WEBVTT

00:03.470 --> 00:04.440
Wait!

00:06.440 --> 00:10.750
We, the elves of Lothdor, 
will not forget our debt to you.

00:10.750 --> 00:14.650
I hereby swear to our 
ancestral god, Rhea Silvia,

00:15.120 --> 00:19.260
that we will return the favor one day.

00:20.190 --> 00:24.370
I pray the blessings of the virtuous 
gods and the spirits of courage

00:24.370 --> 00:27.320
will be with you as you go.

00:35.300 --> 00:40.850
The Faraway Paladin

00:37.140 --> 00:40.850
<b><u>The Lord of the Rust Mountains</u></b>

01:58.130 --> 02:04.350
A Warrior's Fire

02:10.470 --> 02:11.890
Ugh.

02:12.270 --> 02:14.030
Wouldn't want to be in here too long.

02:14.030 --> 02:17.070
We were right not to use fire.

02:17.070 --> 02:19.020
The air is stagnant.

02:19.320 --> 02:22.850
Sir William cast a spell of 
poison resistance on all of us,

02:22.850 --> 02:24.740
but it's still a nasty feeling.

02:25.380 --> 02:27.820
Poor visibility, too.

02:27.820 --> 02:31.050
The possibility of enemy encounters 
and traps is terrifying.

02:31.270 --> 02:33.300
We are up against demons, after all.

02:33.780 --> 02:37.540
Some crawl on the walls and ceilings. 
Some even have wings.

02:38.200 --> 02:42.730
Keep that in the back of your mind as we 
keep our focus in front and to our sides.

02:43.250 --> 02:46.450
We'll post a guard occasionally 
and take short breaks.

02:46.450 --> 02:47.290
Right.

02:55.590 --> 02:56.520
Stop.

02:58.560 --> 03:00.840
There's a trap. I'll disarm it.

03:02.840 --> 03:05.010
Do you know where we are?

03:05.010 --> 03:07.340
We should be coming up on the Hall of Stone.

03:07.730 --> 03:10.470
The paths diverge drastically from there.

03:12.320 --> 03:14.990
All good. Let's go.

03:15.250 --> 03:15.980
Yeah.

03:20.290 --> 03:22.010
Surprising.

03:22.260 --> 03:26.000
Yes. We weren't attacked 
by demons even once.

03:26.230 --> 03:28.420
Could that mean... well...

03:28.420 --> 03:33.680
that the dragon and the demons 
are not actually a monolith?

03:33.680 --> 03:36.020
We can't say that for certain yet.

03:36.020 --> 03:39.580
Maybe they're all assembled in 
the Hall of Stone just ahead

03:39.580 --> 03:41.520
and are waiting to ambush us.

03:41.520 --> 03:45.950
But if there's no ambush, 
it'll mean Al's right.

03:45.950 --> 03:46.730
Wait.

03:52.530 --> 03:53.910
What is it?

03:54.270 --> 03:55.390
I hear something.

03:55.810 --> 03:59.720
The sound of clanking metal... 
and footsteps coming and going.

04:00.410 --> 04:01.930
Is it an ambush?

04:01.930 --> 04:03.170
I don't know.

04:03.170 --> 04:06.430
All I can say for sure is 
that something's out there.

04:06.430 --> 04:09.810
Um... Does that mean this is, uh...

04:09.810 --> 04:10.590
Yeah.

04:13.140 --> 04:16.800
Ghelreis and I will go in 
first with our shields up.

04:16.800 --> 04:19.140
Menel, back us up from the corridor.

04:19.140 --> 04:21.060
Al and Reystov, stand by.

04:21.060 --> 04:22.690
We'll watch for our chance to charge in.

05:08.640 --> 05:13.510
Ah, we have dwarfs. Humans and an elf, too.

05:13.510 --> 05:16.300
I thought Lothdor had fallen.

05:16.300 --> 05:17.980
Did this one escape?

05:17.980 --> 05:20.930
Don't worry, brethren. You're safe here.

05:28.090 --> 05:30.520
How goes the battle?

05:30.520 --> 05:32.380
You must have had a rough time.

05:36.490 --> 05:37.930
Everyone...

05:37.930 --> 05:41.530
Oh! I know you! You're Ghelreis!

05:41.530 --> 05:43.290
I thought you got out.

05:44.610 --> 05:49.190
Did you get out and then come back? 
That's just like you.

05:49.190 --> 05:51.610
You've got guts, though.

05:51.610 --> 05:54.290
You'll add the strength of 
a hundred to our ranks.

05:54.290 --> 05:56.000
Fight with us!

06:05.180 --> 06:06.280
Al...

06:07.360 --> 06:11.180
I think... I should be the one to tell them.

06:22.590 --> 06:24.950
King Aurvangr?

06:24.950 --> 06:29.480
No, this isn't the king. 
He should be in the throne room.

06:31.630 --> 06:33.620
My name is Vindalfr!

06:35.170 --> 06:40.130
I carry within me the blood of Aurvangr, 
the last king of the Iron Country!

06:40.130 --> 06:43.180
The last? He is not the last!

06:43.180 --> 06:47.370
We are still here. 
The Iron Country has not yet fallen.

06:49.070 --> 06:53.360
That is a fine estacade. 
You are well-prepared.

06:53.680 --> 06:57.550
I can tell you have continued 
to repair and improve it.

06:57.980 --> 07:01.720
That's right. 
It is the pinnacle of our technology.

07:01.720 --> 07:04.810
We will not allow the demons to enter here.

07:06.430 --> 07:07.670
I see.

07:08.700 --> 07:09.740
But...

07:14.850 --> 07:17.990
Despite all this, 
the Iron Country has fallen!

07:17.990 --> 07:20.320
All of the warriors died!

07:20.320 --> 07:22.790
The great King Aurvangr died!

07:22.790 --> 07:24.970
Lothdor has tragically withered away,

07:24.970 --> 07:28.010
and the Iron Country 
is now the Rust Mountains,

07:28.010 --> 07:29.960
where a dragon and demons lurk!

07:30.250 --> 07:33.560
That... cannot be.

07:34.060 --> 07:38.030
The Iron Country... cannot fall...

07:38.030 --> 07:39.980
You know it to be true!

07:39.980 --> 07:43.660
Do not avert your eyes from the 
truth, brave dwarf warriors!

07:47.400 --> 07:51.240
My grandfather, Aurvangr, 
struck back at the evil dragon

07:51.240 --> 07:53.220
and took one of his eyes!

07:53.220 --> 07:56.360
It was a heroic act celebrated 
by the gods themselves!

07:56.360 --> 08:01.710
And I, Vindalfr, have committed 
myself to carrying on his heroism,

08:02.590 --> 08:05.400
alongside the heroes of the present day!

08:05.960 --> 08:08.770
It is true that the Iron Country has fallen.

08:08.770 --> 08:14.670
But I pray they may now sit at the 
side of our ancestral god Blaze,

08:14.670 --> 08:17.960
as well as that of Gracefeel, 
goddess of light!

08:18.430 --> 08:24.440
I hereby swear on the names of all the 
virtuous gods and our ancestral spirits

08:24.440 --> 08:28.450
that I will bring back the Iron 
Country's former prosperity!

08:28.750 --> 08:30.690
The kiln fires have not yet gone out!

08:30.690 --> 08:34.370
Their flames will spread, 
burning off all the rust,

08:34.370 --> 08:38.450
and the Rust Mountains will be 
the Iron Mountains once more!

08:45.090 --> 08:49.260
So... please rest now.

08:50.560 --> 08:53.950
You have all done more than enough.

09:26.050 --> 09:29.300
Young master... Well said.

09:29.720 --> 09:33.990
Let us drive away the demons 
and see your promise through.

09:34.520 --> 09:38.470
I will protect you even if 
it costs me my ancient life.

09:38.470 --> 09:40.990
I wouldn't exchange that for your life.

09:42.080 --> 09:45.670
There is still much I 
need to learn from you.

09:45.670 --> 09:47.610
About these mountains...

09:48.550 --> 09:50.320
and about how to fight.

09:52.480 --> 09:57.210
Who makes pain-in-the-ass promises 
about rebuilding nations?

09:57.210 --> 09:58.650
Talk about dumb.

09:58.650 --> 10:01.690
Unlike the vows you and Sir Will made,

10:01.690 --> 10:05.280
at least mine has an end in sight, 
so it's not as dumb as yours.

10:07.400 --> 10:11.580
We must win first, and then survive.

10:11.580 --> 10:12.360
Yes.

10:13.300 --> 10:16.050
Sir Will, I apologize for the delay.

10:16.050 --> 10:18.310
Let us proceed. Your orders?

10:18.800 --> 10:21.420
You don't need to call me "Sir" anymore.

10:22.620 --> 10:25.040
I can't make a king be my thane.

10:25.040 --> 10:26.220
But that's...

10:26.680 --> 10:30.220
No. You are still Sir Will,

10:30.650 --> 10:34.340
the peerless knight that 
I admire and respect.

10:35.510 --> 10:38.920
I see. I guess I can't stop you, then.

10:40.890 --> 10:43.850
That was very commendable. Well done.

10:44.940 --> 10:47.500
I'm sure they all felt blessed, as well.

10:47.500 --> 10:48.360
Yes!

10:49.880 --> 10:51.470
U-Um...

10:51.470 --> 10:55.880
Should I be somewhat grateful to 
the god of the undead, as well?

10:55.880 --> 10:57.290
Uh...

10:57.980 --> 11:01.210
J-Just a little bit couldn't hurt, I guess?

11:11.940 --> 11:14.230
I know it was necessary,

11:14.230 --> 11:16.510
but it looks like we lost 
a little too much time.

11:21.100 --> 11:22.650
Let's go.

11:23.040 --> 11:24.670
We must take back the Iron Country,

11:25.040 --> 11:27.190
the nation of the dwarfs.

11:30.210 --> 11:32.820
By the light of Gracefeel!

12:01.070 --> 12:03.250
Go right at the next branch!

12:03.250 --> 12:04.080
Right!

12:06.200 --> 12:09.570
Having such rough-and-tumble guys 
out in front makes this easy.

12:12.120 --> 12:13.550
Will, doing okay?

12:13.550 --> 12:16.720
Yeah. There's not that much 
pressure from the rear.

12:16.720 --> 12:18.520
I can handle it on my own.

12:19.240 --> 12:21.590
Just fine covering our 
rear on your own, huh?

12:21.590 --> 12:24.560
You're as brilliant as ever, I see.

12:24.850 --> 12:26.430
I'm really not.

12:27.140 --> 12:28.760
I'm not alone, after all.

12:31.660 --> 12:33.570
We will soon reach the Hall of Light.

12:33.970 --> 12:36.690
The dragon is likely in the 
Great Cavern just beyond there.

12:37.380 --> 12:40.950
I imagine the demons will be waiting 
to intercept us in the Hall of Light.

12:41.330 --> 12:46.240
It is the throne room where the great 
King Aurvangr delivered his last speech.

12:47.060 --> 12:48.700
We have to take it back.

12:49.120 --> 12:51.440
Yeah. Let's take it back!

12:51.440 --> 12:53.020
Well, if you say so.

12:53.020 --> 12:55.220
I'll back you up, at least.

12:55.220 --> 13:00.210
Yeah. Everything that was 
stolen should be taken back.

13:08.420 --> 13:09.510
Is that...

13:32.240 --> 13:33.800
I think that's...

13:34.400 --> 13:37.460
The general... Scarabaeus.

13:44.570 --> 13:47.900
Sir Will, please let me handle him.

13:49.260 --> 13:52.450
Al... no, Vindalfr.

13:52.920 --> 13:54.220
I wish you luck.

13:54.220 --> 13:55.580
Thank you.

13:57.410 --> 13:58.700
Wha... Hey!

13:58.700 --> 13:59.720
It's all right, Menel.

14:00.420 --> 14:01.480
Let him go.

14:01.480 --> 14:02.450
Hang on a minute!

14:02.710 --> 14:05.450
That's a general! 
It's way out of his league!

14:08.540 --> 14:09.700
Still...

14:10.110 --> 14:12.110
This is Al's battle.

14:12.440 --> 14:15.940
A king's battle for his throne.

14:34.380 --> 14:36.650
I don't like that look on its face.

14:36.930 --> 14:38.510
It's strong.

14:38.510 --> 14:41.790
You're gonna let him die for 
some warrior's hang-up?

14:41.790 --> 14:44.520
You're not the only one 
who taught him, you know.

14:45.030 --> 14:48.020
Yes, but either way...

14:48.270 --> 14:52.030
I doubt we'll have a chance to interfere.

14:58.580 --> 14:59.950
Guess that's what you meant!

15:05.430 --> 15:08.940
Hey, Al! If you can't handle it, 
just stay alive until we win!

15:08.940 --> 15:10.180
Don't die!

15:10.450 --> 15:14.290
Thank you, Sir Menel. But...

15:14.930 --> 15:17.660
I will win! I will beat him!

15:17.660 --> 15:20.720
I swear on her light, and on his flames,

15:21.420 --> 15:24.300
that this denizen of the 
mountains will defeat you!

15:25.070 --> 15:28.320
<b>We will slay you all! Taste the axe of the dwarfs!</b>

16:07.280 --> 16:08.470
Currere, Oleum!

16:07.480 --> 16:08.480
<b>Run, Oil</b>

16:28.590 --> 16:30.120
A blessing?!

16:38.080 --> 16:40.570
<i>I want to use Words that erase magic, but...</i>

16:42.840 --> 16:43.660
Damn it!

16:52.280 --> 16:52.780
Al!

16:53.410 --> 16:55.770
It's... all right.

16:57.530 --> 17:00.310
I will... not lose.

17:00.310 --> 17:05.300
On my vow... and on the 
hopes of my brethren...

17:06.270 --> 17:08.460
I will...

17:12.620 --> 17:16.140
take back our homeland!

17:40.420 --> 17:44.810
I'll be taking back what you stole from us!

18:07.740 --> 18:11.240
<i>They go into battle with 
their very souls on fire. {ep3 final}</i>

18:11.860 --> 18:13.850
<i>They don't fear death. {/ep3}</i>

18:14.960 --> 18:17.440
I've taken out the enemy general!

18:22.230 --> 18:25.030
It's not over yet, Al! 
Keep it up a little longer!

18:25.030 --> 18:26.050
Of course!

18:34.850 --> 18:37.750
<i>We're nearing our limit.</i>

18:39.630 --> 18:42.630
<i>But this is their last commander!</i>

18:47.400 --> 18:48.650
Discede!

18:47.430 --> 18:48.390
<b>Leave</b>

18:59.680 --> 19:02.480
Ghelreis, stand guard.

19:02.480 --> 19:03.580
Right.

19:03.580 --> 19:04.820
Let's heal you.

19:21.910 --> 19:25.330
Man, I really thought we were all dead meat.

19:25.330 --> 19:29.440
Five of us charging into the demons' 
base was definitely reckless.

19:30.630 --> 19:33.280
Well done, my man. You did great.

19:33.280 --> 19:36.100
N-No, I didn't really...

19:42.320 --> 19:46.420
You took it all back. 
The mountains and the crown.

19:46.420 --> 19:48.670
No, not quite.

19:49.160 --> 19:52.440
I haven't taken <i>everything</i> back yet.

19:52.920 --> 19:54.800
Yeah, you're right.

19:54.800 --> 19:57.750
But as soon as I do,

19:57.750 --> 20:00.540
I'd like you to put this crown on my head.

20:00.540 --> 20:04.910
Huh? Isn't that something only 
high-ranking clergymen can do?

20:05.160 --> 20:06.960
Isn't that what you are?

20:06.960 --> 20:07.860
Oh.

20:12.300 --> 20:13.150
Let's go.

20:13.150 --> 20:13.960
Wait.

20:14.690 --> 20:16.070
Look over there.

20:17.320 --> 20:19.880
Scarabaeus's body is gone...

20:19.880 --> 20:22.570
Hm? But his head is still here.

20:22.570 --> 20:25.280
Demons are supposed to turn 
to dust when they die.

20:25.280 --> 20:27.320
Yet even after being beheaded, he...

20:27.700 --> 20:28.850
Let's track him.

20:33.820 --> 20:36.110
He's heading toward the Great Cavern.

20:36.110 --> 20:38.050
To get help from the dragon?

20:38.050 --> 20:42.200
He may also just be wandering around 
blindly on reflexive bodily movements.

20:43.140 --> 20:45.670
<i>The miasma is getting thicker and thicker.</i>

20:46.640 --> 20:48.090
Everyone, be careful.

20:56.770 --> 20:59.320
This is the Great Cavern.

21:01.020 --> 21:02.280
Let's get searching.

21:14.320 --> 21:15.160
There he is!

21:17.430 --> 21:19.000
What is he...

21:33.560 --> 21:36.240
So weak...

21:53.610 --> 21:59.540
Welcome to my bedchamber.

23:35.600 --> 23:40.010
The Lord of the Rust Mountains
